  "id": "Compound::DB00259 - Gene::760",
  "verbalization": "Sulfanilamide appears to interact with calcium ions (Ca2) through a series of biochemical pathways that involve calcium-binding proteins and enzymatic activities. The evidence suggests that Sulfanilamide binds to Ca6 or Ca9, which then participate in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide or carbonate dehydratase activity. These processes are ultimately linked to Ca2, indicating a potential role for Sulfanilamide in modulating calcium-dependent enzymatic functions. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Sulfanilamide influences calcium homeostasis, though the exact nature of the interaction remains partially inferred. The evidence supports a dependency on calcium ions in the enzymatic processes mediated by Sulfanilamide, suggesting a broader role in cellular metabolism.",
